KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ reused instances: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static_assert condition could not be evaluated
--
CBMC re-instantiated an alias, concept or variable template specialization
at each use; it now reuses the instance (25% less type-checking time for
std::print).  A guard: the reused instances give the same results, also
after substitution failures and from another scope.  (f(1.0) is checked at
run time only: CBMC does not evaluate it in a constant expression.)
